{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n`src/rebar/_store/event_append.py` is 791 LOC — only 9 under the 800 hard cap, i.e. one feature away from breaking the module-size gate. It mixes the low-level git **subprocess primitives** with the public append/commit **API** and git-failure **recovery**. Zero in-progress contention. Flagged by audit ae1b (size/near-cap risk).\n\n## Approach (extract the git-primitive LEAF; keep API+recovery together — behavior-preserving, zero test edits)\nExtract ONLY the bottom layer — the git subprocess primitives — into a new leaf module `event_append_git.py`, and slim `event_append.py` to the API + recovery. This buys real headroom below the cap and gives git-primitive changes one home, WITHOUT disturbing the monkeypatch/test seams that couple the API and recovery layers.\n\nWhy NOT also split recovery into its own module: the recovery routine `_recover_from_invalid_object` calls `_git_add` on its re-add path, and `tests/interfaces/store/test_event_append_transient_retry.py:308-320` monkeypatches `event_append._git_add` with a wrapper that must be observed by BOTH the happy-path add in `stage_and_commit` (event_append.py:423) AND that recovery re-add (recovery region ~:772) from a SINGLE `setattr`. Keeping `stage_and_commit` and `_recover_from_invalid_object` in the same module means both resolve `_git_add` through the `event_append` module global, so one patch reaches both — behavior identical to today. Splitting recovery out would put the two callers in different namespaces and silently break that test's re-add coupling. This is a deliberate G6 seam choice, not incompleteness.\n\n1. Extract **git subprocess primitives** → new `src/rebar/_store/event_append_git.py` (~180 LOC): `_run_git` (event_append.py:246), `_git_add` (:263), `_git_commit` (:287), `_git_rm` (:312), `_git_commit_paths` (:324), `_with_transient_add_retry` (:205), `_with_transient_head_retry`, `_is_transient_add_error` (:197), plus EVERY module-level constant these depend on and that nothing in the retained code uses: `_GIT_TIMEOUT`, `_TRANSIENT_ADD_MARKERS` (:188), `_GIT_ADD_ATTEMPTS` (:193), `_GIT_ADD_BACKOFF_S` (:194). This module owns the sole `import subprocess` (and `import time` for the backoff).\n2. `event_append.py` retains the **public API + validation + recovery**: `StoreError`, `event_filename`, `_ensure_initialized`, `_validate_event`, `_prepare_event`, `delete_events`, `stage_and_commit`, `batch_stage_and_commit`, `write_and_push`, `batch_write_and_push`, `_maybe_enrich_drain`, and the recovery routines `_recover_from_unmerged`/`_recover_from_invalid_object`/`_is_invalid_object_error`/`_rollback_batch`/`_restore_paths`/`_unstage`/`_silent_unlink`/`_staged_index_paths` with their constants `_REGENERABLE_PREFIX`/`_INVALID_OBJECT_MARKERS`; keeps the existing `_INDEX_LOCK_STALE_S` re-export (:45). It imports the git primitives from `event_append_git` as local bindings and calls them by bare name so the module-global lookup stays monkeypatch-visible. Target ≈ 615 LOC (down from 791 → ~185 LOC of cap headroom).\n\n## Preserve every test/consumer binding via re-export — NO test edits (G1G2)\nThe suite reaches relocated symbols and the `subprocess` seam through the `event_append` namespace, via BOTH dotted (`event_append.NAME`) and string-literal (`setattr/getattr(event_append, \"NAME\")`) forms. The COMPLETE relocated-symbol reference set, enumerated with a two-pass grep over the dotted `event_append.NAME` and string-literal `setattr/getattr(event_append, \"NAME\")` forms (see the final AC for the exact portable command), is:\n- `event_append.subprocess.run` monkeypatch (13 sites across c2ba, delete_events, write_index_reset_on_failure, batch_write, import_batch_resume, transient_retry, index_lock) — preserved because `event_append.subprocess` and `event_append_git.subprocess` are the SAME cached module object; re-exporting `subprocess` keeps the seam patch-visible for the relocated `_run_git`/`_git_add`.\n- `event_append._run_git(...)` direct calls + `event_append._GIT_TIMEOUT` reads (c2ba) and `event_append._is_transient_add_error` — resolved by re-exporting those names.\n- `setattr(event_append, \"_git_add\", …)` (transient_retry:318) — resolved because `_git_add` is re-exported into `event_append` AND its only in-repo callers (`stage_and_commit`, `_recover_from_invalid_object`) live in `event_append` and call it by bare name → both observe the patch.\n- Names that are NOT relocated and need nothing: `stage_and_commit`/`batch_stage_and_commit`/`write_and_push`/`_maybe_enrich_drain` (push_callers, sidecar) and `getattr(event_append, \"_INDEX_LOCK_STALE_S\")` (txn_index_lock:21, index_lock:41) all stay in `event_append`.\n\nRe-export shim in `event_append.py` (mirrors the existing `_INDEX_LOCK_STALE_S` precedent at :45):\n```\nfrom .event_append_git import (  # noqa: F401 — re-export for namespace/monkeypatch-seam stability\n    _run_git, _git_add, _git_commit, _git_rm, _git_commit_paths,\n    _is_transient_add_error, _with_transient_add_retry, _with_transient_head_retry,\n    _GIT_TIMEOUT, subprocess,\n)\n```\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_store/event_append.py` — remove git primitives; retain API + recovery; add the re-export shim.\n- `src/rebar/_store/event_append_git.py` — NEW (git subprocess primitives + their constants; owns `import subprocess`/`import time`).\n\n## Verification (behavior-preserving refactor)\n- `event_append.py` well under the 800 cap with real headroom; module-size + type + lint gates green (re-export carries `# noqa: F401`).\n- `event_append_git` is a leaf: imports neither `event_append` nor any sibling.\n- Store/concurrency suites plus the eight namespace-coupled tests above pass UNCHANGED via the re-exports.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `wc -l src/rebar/_store/event_append.py` ≤ 640 (down from 791; ≥ 160 LOC of headroom under the 800 cap); `event_append_git.py` ≥ 100 LOC.\n- [ ] `event_append_git` is a leaf, verified by `python -c \"s=open('src/rebar/_store/event_append_git.py').read(); assert 'from .event_append' not in s and 'import event_append' not in s\"` and `python -c \"import rebar._store.event_append\"` succeeding.\n- [ ] All prior bindings resolve unchanged (public + re-exported privates/seam): `python -c \"from rebar._store.event_append import stage_and_commit, write_and_push, batch_write_and_push, delete_events, StoreError; import rebar._store.event_append as e; e._run_git; e._git_add; e._GIT_TIMEOUT; e.subprocess; e._recover_from_invalid_object\"`.\n- [ ] Full default suite green with NO test edits. Re-export completeness is a checked invariant covering BOTH access forms — with `refs` defined as `{ grep -rhoE 'event_append\\.(_[A-Za-z_]+|subprocess)' tests/ --include=*.py | sed 's/^event_append\\.//'; grep -rhoE '(set|get)attr\\(event_append, \"[^\"]+\"' tests/ --include=*.py | sed -E 's/.*\"([^\"]+)\"/\\1/'; } | sort -u`, the command `comm -23 <(refs) <(printf '%s\\n' _run_git _git_add _git_commit _git_rm _git_commit_paths _is_transient_add_error _with_transient_add_retry _with_transient_head_retry _GIT_TIMEOUT subprocess _ensure_initialized _maybe_enrich_drain _INDEX_LOCK_STALE_S stage_and_commit batch_stage_and_commit write_and_push | sort -u)` produces NO output (every name any test binds via the `event_append` namespace is either re-exported from `event_append_git` or a symbol retained in `event_append`)."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786233820779805001,"uuid":"ab0c3265-91ee-453b-8c0b-9f4be7d6b4b0"}